#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md:6
msgid "Unsafe is dangerous"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md:8
msgid ""
"“Use-after-free (UAF), integer overflows, and out of bounds (OOB) reads/"
"writes comprise 90% of vulnerabilities with OOB being the most common.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md:11
msgid ""
"\\--- **Jeff Vander Stoep and Chong Zang**, Google. \"[Queue the Hardening "
"Enhancements](https://security.googleblog.com/2019/05/queue-hardening-"
"enhancements.html)\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md:18
msgid ""
"“The software industry has gathered lots of evidence that unsafe code is "
"difficult to write correctly and creates very serious problems.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md:21
msgid ""
"“The issues in this list are eliminated by Rust. The unsafe keyword lets "
"them back into your source code.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md:24
msgid "“Be careful.”"
msgstr ""
